&lt;p&gt;This writeup is for &lt;code&gt;Cupids Matchmaker&lt;/code&gt;, a room in TryHackMe (THM) for Valentine&amp;rsquo;s 2026 Event. This room focuses on XSS Vulnerability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) is a condition when a web application accepts untrusted data from a user and sends it to a web browser without proper sanitazion. This allows an attacker to inject and execute malicious scripts (usually JavaScript) within the victim&amp;rsquo;s website. There are 3 main types of XXS. They are Stored, Reflected, and Blind XSS.&lt;/p&gt;</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="http://localhost:1313/hagen-kwik-lab/writeups/cupids_matchmaker/featured.jpg"/></item></channel></rss>